{:lexicon 1,
 :id "com.etzhayyim.ooyake.officeHolder",
 :description
 "An OBSERVATIONAL MIRROR record of the CURRENT PUBLIC OFFICE HOLDER of a government unit already present in the atlas (ADR-2607253000; G6 as amended 2026-07-25). It records exactly one thing: that a named person publicly holds a named office in a named body, since a date, per a cited source. CONSTITUTIONAL SCOPE — what this record may NEVER carry: private/home contact, address, private life, family, finances, health, movements, schedule, religion, party membership, or any individual who is not a public office holder. Those fields do not exist in this lexicon and are not requested from any upstream source, so they cannot be present-but-empty; they are unrepresentable. G10 (civic wayfinding, NEVER a target-list) binds every row: this answers 'who holds this office' for civic wayfinding and accountability, never 'where is this person'. G11 (politically neutral): no evaluation, ranking, score or judgement of the person — holding an office is a fact, not a verdict. Non-fabrication (G5): `sourcing` + `provenance` + `lastVerified` mandatory; a term with an end date is NOT current and is not emitted. Projection of the :gov.person/* kotoba vocabulary; `unit` always resolves to an existing :gov.unit/id.",
 :defs
 {:main
  {:type "record",
   :key "any",
   :record
   {:type "object",
    :required
    ["personId"
     "unit"
     "roleEn"
     "nameEn"
     "sourcing"
     "provenance"
     "lastVerified"],
    :properties
    {:personId
     {:type "string",
      :description "→ :gov.person/id — person.<unit-suffix>.<role-slug>, deterministic"},
     :unit
     {:type "string",
      :description "→ :gov.unit/id — the atlas body whose office this is. ALWAYS an existing unit; office holders are never recorded for a body the atlas does not already carry, so there are no orphan person rows."},
     :unitWikidata
     {:type "string",
      :description "the unit's QID — the key the holder was looked up by, kept so the derivation is re-checkable"},
     :jurisdiction
     {:type "string", :description "ISO3 of the unit, denormalized for filtering"},
     :roleEn
     {:type "string",
      :description "the office in English, derived from the Wikidata property that related person to body (head of state / head of government / chairperson / director / chief executive / officeholder). Deliberately the STRUCTURAL relation rather than a free-text title: it says exactly what evidence exists."},
     :roleProperty
     {:type "string",
      :description "the raw Wikidata property slug behind roleEn — provenance for the role claim itself"},
     :nameEn {:type "string", :description "name as labelled in English"},
     :nameNative {:type "string", :description "P1559 native-language name when one is published"},
     :since {:type "string", :description "term start (P580), ISO date. Absent when the source records none — never guessed."},
     :officialUrl {:type "string", :description "the BODY's official URL (not a personal site) — the public place this office is described"},
     :wikidata {:type "string", :description "the person's QID — the citation, so any row can be re-checked at source"},
     :sourcing
     {:type "string",
      :enum ["authoritative" "third-party" "representative"],
      :description "G5 — where the CLAIM came from, not how much we trust it. `authoritative`: the office-holding was seen on the authority's own page (`sourceUrl` cites it). `third-party`: real, but taken from an aggregator (Wikidata) and NOT checked against the authority — this is the honest default for anything the atlas has not independently confirmed. `representative`: illustrative, never counted as coverage. `third-party` was added 2026-07-25 (ADR-2607253400) because every office-holder row was claiming `authoritative` while carrying `provenance: wikidata`, which asserted a primary check that had never happened."},
     :sourceUrl
     {:type "string",
      :description "the authority's own page on which this person was found holding this office — present only on `authoritative` rows, and the thing that makes them authoritative. Absent means nobody has confirmed it against the government's own publication yet, which is a coverage gap rather than a doubt about the person."},
     :provenance {:type "string", :description "where this row came from, e.g. \"wikidata\""},
     :lastVerified
     {:type "string",
      :description "G5 — the date this was actually read from the source. An office holder is a CHANGING fact; without this date the row asserts more than it knows. A stale row is a dated row, not a false one."}}}}}}
